//            matched arms R271 L16 removes."; its lines are re-wrapped;
//            (5) HOW(IF_THEN): "to the witness verdict" became "to the comparison's verdict, which is not the obligation's
//            discharge"; its lines are re-wrapped;
//            (6) HOW(BECAUSE): the quotation "the events are its record" with its attribution is removed, and "R264 L19–L21"
//            leaves the BECAUSE line; its lines are re-wrapped;
//            (7) WHAT(MAYBE): a condition is added for a captured effect that is neither ASSIGN nor RETAIN_SITE, and a
//            sentence saying an envelope names exactly the junctions its flag is incident to; "L18" joins R271 L17 and "R270
//            L14" joins the BECAUSE line; its lines are re-wrapped;
//            (8) FOR_WHAT(MUST_LET): "Shown so far on offline replay of the fact-commit routines only; on a card execution it
//            is to be witnessed." became "The first is shown so far on offline replay of the fact-commit routines only; both
//            are to be witnessed on a card execution.";
//            (9) HOW(MORE_LESS): "an execution's capture does" became "an execution's capture MUST";
//            (10) R_RECORD reading: "not the per-junction counts" became "R272 does not report the per-junction counts",
//            with the sentence break moved.
//            The seed's cells are the same 31; the obligation block, the terminal, the encoding block and every vector do
//            not change.
// CHANGE 0.1.6 (unpromoted): Independent check of v0.1.5 (RUN_RECORD 47AF01C0…2C7F): CHECK_FORM no NO; two NOT_SAME.
//            First: CHANGE 0.1.5 did not name these changes of v0.1.5: the obligation line gained "on the bound card"; the
//            restriction-readings header's list became "R264, R265, R271, R272"; the held list replaced PRIOR_v0.1.3.mal and
//            PRIOR_RUN_RECORD_V013.md by the v0.1.4 names (the note said "extended"); the attribution sentence for R265, R270,
//            R271 and R272 changed; the BECAUSE lines of the six cells of its members (a) to (c) changed; HOW(BECAUSE) gained
//            "An edit is realized by a native ASSIGN field effect; the heat is what that discharge causes." Its member (e)
//            "to the same effect" meant the restatement of (a) to (d), not the cells' v0.1.4 content, which those cells no
//            longer carry. Second: the R_SHED_CLASS reading cited R264 L35–L43 for the ASSIGN identification, which those
//            lines do not name. Changed here:
//            (a) R_SHED_CLASS reading and WHAT(NEAR_FAR): the candidate is cited at R270 L43–L45 (Claude, PROPOSE), and the
//            reading says which sentence of R264 is not relied on;
//            (b) WHAT(NO) gains the bound-card condition WHAT(IF_THEN) has and reads NO only where the effect of every
//            incident flag is captured; WHAT(IF_THEN) marks the SUBSTRATE reading as this specification's own, replacing
//            R264 L53–L54's; WHAT(MAYBE) states the not-observed rule per junction;
//            (c) HOW(BECAUSE): one sentence added on the standing of the retained ASSIGN facts;
//            (d) HOW(MUST_LET), FOR_WHAT(MUST_LET), HOW(MORE_LESS): stated as MUST, with the offline scope; the run record's
//            list is R272 L32–L33's in full;
//            (e) the obligation line places R_CUSTODY under the binding to the tick; R_EVENTS, R_ENVELOPE and R_CUSTODY carry
//            the items of R271 L16, L18 and R272 L32–L33 they omitted; REQUIRED names the four restrictions a run record
//            carries and says R_SHED_CLASS is not one of them;
//            (f) restriction readings: the header's list; R_RECORD (what the offline capture reproduces); R_ENVELOPE (one
//            sentence added); R_SHED_CLASS as in (a);
//            (g) the BECAUSE lines of WHAT(NEAR_FAR), WHAT(IF_THEN), WHAT(MAYBE), HOW(BECAUSE), FOR_WHAT(MUST_LET) and
//            HOW(MORE_LESS); those of WHAT(NO) and HOW(MUST_LET) keep their words and move to a line of their own;
//            (h) contact R268 added for Devon's 10:27 statement, with ORIGIN's pointer to it, the held list (R268; the
//            v0.1.5 names replace the v0.1.4 names) and the attribution sentence.
//            The seed's cells are the same 31; the terminal, the encoding block and every vector do not change.
// CHANGE 0.1.5 (unpromoted): The witness is restated from a reader's column to the fold's native events on the bound card. Sources: Codex's reads of
//            the runtime (R270, R271), its offline implementation (R272), and Devon 2026-11-13 11:02 "The measure isnt the
//            thing the thing causes the heat" (R272 L10). v0.1.4's independent check (RUN_RECORD 3EEFCA8A…711C) had no NO and no
//            NOT_SAME; this version changes the object, not a defect of form. Changed: (a) SUBSTRATE(v) is now read from
//            captured ASSIGN / RETAIN_SITE field effects through their junction envelopes, on an execution bound to the card
//            (WHAT(NO), WHAT(IF_THEN), the encoding block); (b) a measurement is never the witness (FOR_WHAT(THIS), HOW(NO)
//            route (c), WHAT(MUST_LET)); (c) HOW(BECAUSE) no longer says the substrate changes a stored reading: the runtime
//            appends and overwrites nothing; (d) the restrictions R_CONTROL, R_ACCOUNT, R_RESOLUTION and R_RUN_RECORD are
//            replaced by R_EVENTS, R_ENVELOPE, R_CUSTODY and R_SHED_CLASS, with their readings; R_RECORD's reading is
//            extended; (e) the cells WHAT(THIS), HOW(THIS), WHAT(INSIDE_OUTSIDE), WHAT(NEAR_FAR), HOW(CAN_CANNOT),
//            WHAT(MAYBE), HOW(MUST_LET), FOR_WHAT(MUST_LET), HOW(MORE_LESS), WHAT(GOES_WITH) and HOW(GOES_WITH) are reworded
//            to the same effect, with their BECAUSE lines; (f) ORIGIN, three contacts (R270, R271, R272) and the held list
//            are extended. The seed's cells are the same 31; the terminal and every vector's expected output do not change.
// CHANGE 0.1.4 (unpromoted): Independent check of v0.1.3 (RUN_RECORD F6C740FD…FC9E): CHECK_FORM no NO; one NOT_SAME: CHANGE 0.1.3 did not say that
//            the words "from the ledger" stand again in the second-vector sentence of the encoding block (v0.1.3 restored
//            them). Changed here: (a) each of the second to sixth vectors carries its byte values on a line inside its own
//            declaration; (b) the SUPERSEDES line names v0.1.3; (c) the held list names PRIOR_v0.1.3.mal and
//            PRIOR_RUN_RECORD_V013.md. No vector's expected output changes.
// CHANGE 0.1.3 (unpromoted): Independent check of v0.1.2 (RUN_RECORD B817B893…4A62): CHECK_FORM no NO; one NOT_SAME: CHANGE 0.1.2 did not name two
//            changes of v0.1.2: HOW(IF_THEN) dropped "the verdict text does not", and the vector notes replaced "are not an
//            input of the comparison and get no verdict" by "a realization MUST refuse them and emit no verdict text",
//            re-ordered their explanation and dropped "from the ledger". Changed here: (a) HOW(IF_THEN) says again that the
//            verdict text carries the verdict word only, and a sixth vector fixes the output for a partly unobserved input;
//            (b) the block before the vectors is headed as the encoding of the vectors' bytes, is explanation throughout, and
//            no longer obliges a refusal: other byte strings are outside this specification; (c) that block says the column
//            order 0..29 is this specification's and is to be confirmed against LEDGER, and no longer says which file carries
//            the numbering; (d) FOR_WHAT(IF_THEN) cites R264 L52–L54 for its first clause; (e) the held list names
//            PRIOR_v0.1.2.mal and PRIOR_RUN_RECORD_V012.md. The expected outputs of the first five vectors do not change.
// CHANGE 0.1.2 (unpromoted): Independent check of v0.1.1 (RUN_RECORD B69C6576…E71B): CHECK_FORM no NO; seven NOT_SAME. Corrected: (a) the thermal
//            citation no longer names a cell no held line names; (b) the precedence is W10D L35, and the cell says this
//            specification applies it to the witness verdict; (c) HOW(NO) route (e) cites R264 L30–L31 for "tick and
//            junctions"; (d) R_RESOLUTION quotes R264 L68 on the fold-level reading; (e) CHANGE 0.1.1 did not name these
//            changes of v0.1.1: the FE / DG promotion sentence, "(PROPOSE)" for R264, "Claude's record of Codex's report" for
//            R265, "LEDGER is named" in the restriction-readings header, and nine doubled blank lines inside the seed block
//            (removed here); it said "all on readings and locators" though three prior items were on layout and the
//            vector rule; and it placed the R_RESOLUTION change under restriction readings though the changed line is the
//            restriction's text. Also from the same check: HOW(THIS) no longer says what identifies the fold; WHAT(INSIDE_OUTSIDE)
//            cites R264 L35–L41; the obligation line says how its five restrictions carry R215's two conditions;
//            FOR_WHAT(IF_THEN) and FOR_WHAT(MUST_LET) quote their lines; the junction numbering is given as R265's report of
//            it; HOW(SAME_NOT_SAME) carries the not-observed case and the vector notes are binding for the vectors; the held
//            list names the prior draft and run record. No vector's expected output changes.
// CHANGE 0.1.1 (unpromoted): Independent check of v0.1.0 (RUN_RECORD 5D9ABBCA…ADD7): CHECK_FORM no NO; nine NOT_SAME and fifteen MAYBE not resting
//            on unheld bytes, all on readings and locators. Corrected: (a) attributions: R215 is Devon's corrections; the FE
//            locator is R264's, the thermal line locator is dropped; (b) cells that said more than their cited lines: HOW(THIS),
//            HOW(MUST_LET), HOW(GOES_WITH), FOR_WHAT(THIS), FOR_WHAT(IF_THEN), FOR_WHAT(MUST_LET), FOR_WHAT(BECAUSE),
//            HOW(CAN_CANNOT), HOW(MORE_LESS), WHAT(TOGETHER_ALONE), HOW(NO) route (e), and R_RUN_RECORD with them;
//            (c) WHAT(BECAUSE), WHAT(SAME_NOT_SAME) and WHAT(INSIDE_OUTSIDE) now say that the held / not-held reading is
//            R264's composition (PROPOSE) and which source carries which half; "INSIDE the ONE" is removed; (d) WHAT(MORE_LESS)
//            quotes FE as R264 quotes it; (e) HOW(IF_THEN) cites the method's precedence and says where unobserved junctions
//            are named; (f) restriction readings: R_RECORD is MAYBE here until the second vector is executed; R_CONTROL uses
//            R265's words; R_ACCOUNT no longer cites a status no record holds; R_RESOLUTION gives the fold-level reading no
//            place in the verdict; (g) vectors: junction order is LEDGER's numbering (no carrier is bound); the comparison's
//            input kind is stated; input_path lines have the example's two fields; a blank line precedes the vector block.
//            Contact W10D added. TARGET no longer names Metis; SCOPE uses "038 untouched". No vector's expected output changes.
// TARGET: the shed of one fold of one world, read on that world's own substrate. J17 first (link 2 → 3, the fold of record 265).
// METHOD: SPEC-MAL-SPECIFICATION-SYSTEM-002 v0.3.1 with W10 (delta 01105ECC…29C2; promoted 2026-11-02 16:47, receipt
//         3D53564CC368F099E10FB3CDF2817AE3E06912D968553516692C898941FCA658, located by Codex; not held here).
// SUBJECT: the witness that a fold's unabsorbed content went to the substrate; not a world transition and not a run.
// SCOPE: folds on which every flag identity persists (the d_G domain). Folds that form new parts are outside this version
//        (R264 L58–L63). 038 untouched; no device or world execution, append, commit or push follows from these bytes.
// ORIGIN: Devon 2026-11-09 00:51 "The shedding is constitutive therefore it must come from the substrate unfolding.";
//         2026-11-13 09:00 "Isnt this supposed to be the substrate?"; 09:04 "Codex continues to put this project in proof loops
//         for things that need to be built or derived or inferred from prior derivation."; 10:27 "the 3070 IS the substrate. We
//         build what we need from the physical substrate to the software." (R268 L7–L8, its first two sentences); 11:02 "The measure isnt the thing the thing causes
//         the heat"
// CONTACTS (exact bytes; registry 66DDE362…1B60 projections for clause locators):
// FPP: contacts/FPP.txt; sha256 897AB3D712DBECC7FA1C2792FFEFFEF37AD59B35FC67D2B2747C436BEE4DA344
// DSUB: contacts/DSUB.md; sha256 D0603C9EB37732B2C4A237C4A41CDCF2CA18210F86A4F7E21BD24B43275F8EAE
// FE: contacts/FE.mal; sha256 E2A87BDC3E5A7AAC7B246F3CBBAF77F141689FCF6270D537ACC059F9E6BB9E9E
// DG: contacts/DG.mal; sha256 3419D528150A8616AF0DCF0446FC59FAD0FF83F1C872C93A0BC8CC70BF0A8718
// THERMAL_V014: contacts/THERMAL_V014.mal; sha256 AF2069CC3BCF1E46C6EC9881E5B2B78BF2BFAE4440D05A536C49644660A5985A
// SAY: contacts/SAY.md; sha256 04A62AFA0B5544C21B1E27A972286DD5BAA96A5EDC3AABFC2BB27DB688C8CD4B
// R215: contacts/R215.md; sha256 10BF6EE1129A05531ECF18B62AE1681555D8714EF9C3C51CADEA303AEE254855
// R264: contacts/R264.md; sha256 9FC10164B571CDE7C405D9CDCB93BB12BEB458DB687B7F8A3423B47827615D8E
// R265: contacts/R265.md; sha256 0174F5D3AE3D21EA9F78E3427648032C98EF429C1FCC7E7DF4EEAB417AF14589
// R268: contacts/R268.md; sha256 9683CD22DA0DF7310C77A23089E4EBF51009F1CEF52E21DBE919EB5D1392A5DF
// R270: contacts/R270.md; sha256 D19A8715B181A7C0627498BB11FD356135E5D7CC980FEB20870EC57E3F341B5E
// R271: contacts/R271.md; sha256 1B468078D013EE072A2CC4C8E202355C587FFFB46C848E4FB9978F11D3C9FC61
// R272: contacts/R272.md; sha256 D7A563AAE84865D45AB0BF7A5C802EE492E19DA7832F42C0E7B048692C9C4D67
// LEDGER: contacts/READING.json; sha256 27BF7FD6913F812DAAF96BF4C7851DECC0180CD3CD169374CFEB217EF6D44AA7
// W10D: contacts/W10D.md; sha256 01105ECC6D60D44C0BF960B27F746E67DB4E1E9B86F2B728FFF4A49AF91829C2
// FE is SPEC-J17-WORLD-FOLD-EFFECT-001 and DG is DECISION_RECORD_FLAG_WORLD_D_G_001; both are promoted per R264 L23, L26
// (their receipts are not held here; DG's own header reads "PROPOSED for DECIDE").
// Held in this package: DSUB, DG, R215, R264, R265, R268, R270, R271, R272, W10D, and as genealogy only (not contacts)
// PRIOR_v0.1.7.mal and PRIOR_RUN_RECORD_V017.md. Not held by Claude: FPP, FE, THERMAL_V014, SAY, LEDGER (LEDGER per
// R265 L7–L9). DSUB is Claude's record of Devon's statement; R215 is Claude's record of Devon's corrections; R264 is Claude's
// construction (PROPOSE); R265, R270, R271 and R272 are Claude's records of Codex's reports (R272 also carries Devon's 11:02 statement); R268 is Claude's forward note, cited for Devon's 10:27 statement only. FE's line locator L126–L128 is the one at R264 L23;
// THERMAL_V014 is cited as R264 L19–L21 quotes it. No obligation's LAW_CLAUSE cites a contact other than FPP.
// SAY rows: S12 ("The obligation discharge (computation) generates heat").

domain SUBSTRATE_WITNESS_OF_SHED;

@propose seed SUBSTRATE_WITNESS_OF_SHED := {
  WHAT(THIS),            // The object is ONE witness: the fold's own native events as executed on the bound card, read against
                         // the record's edit set, for ONE fold of ONE world (J17, link 2 → 3). BECAUSE DSUB L5, R271 L16–L17.
  HOW(THIS),             // LEDGER holds every flag's identity and its before / after reading; the run record carries the card
                         // identity, the executing context and the chain link of the fold. BECAUSE R265 L7–L8, R271 L17.
  FOR_WHAT(THIS),        // "The measure isnt the thing the thing causes the heat": the witness is the event on the substrate;
                         // a measurement is recorded beside it and no verdict depends on it. BECAUSE R272 L10, R271 L16.

  WHAT(SAME_NOT_SAME),   // EDIT := ONE flag entry whose reading is NOT_SAME its reading in the predecessor field (DG L15–L18).
                         // HELD := the readings SAME across the fold; NOT HELD := the predecessor readings at the edits: R264's
                         // composition (PROPOSE). BECAUSE DG L15–L18, R264 L35–L40.
  HOW(SAME_NOT_SAME),    // Per junction v the comparison is SUBSTRATE(v) SAME RECORD(v); both are readings THIS / NO, compared
                         // as exact bytes; a junction not observed has no SUBSTRATE reading and is MAYBE, by name.
                         // BECAUSE R264 L52–L55, DG L23–L24.
  FOR_WHAT(SAME_NOT_SAME), // An observed junction whose two readings are NOT_SAME refutes the witness for that fold. BECAUSE R264 L52–L55.

  WHAT(NO),              // RECORD(v) := NO where no edit is incident to v; SUBSTRATE(v) := NO where the bound card's execution
                         // of the fold captures the field effect of every flag incident to v, at least one, and each is a
                         // RETAIN_SITE effect. NO is a reading; a junction not observed carries no NO.
                         // BECAUSE DG L20–L21, R271 L14, L18, R265 L16, L29.
  HOW(NO),               // Non-discharging routes: (a) reading the fold's records again for the shed, which records do not
                         // hold; (b) taking every discharge event at a junction for the shed; (c) taking a measurement (a
                         // cycle count, a temperature) for the witness; (d) reading a junction that was not observed as NO;
                         // (e) treating the separately checked binding to the fold's tick and junctions and distinction of
                         // shed from discharge activity as the witness without their joint satisfaction on the SAME fold
                         // cannot discharge that joint requirement (FPP :131–138 is a joint accounting clause; its shed is
                         // :138). BECAUSE DSUB L12, R215 L15–L17, R264 L30–L31, R272 L10, R265 L29, FPP.

  WHAT(IF_THEN),         // IF an edit is incident to v THEN RECORD(v) := THIS. IF the bound card's execution of the fold
                         // captures an ASSIGN field effect whose envelope names v THEN SUBSTRATE(v) := THIS. Both readings of
                         // SUBSTRATE(v), THIS here and NO in WHAT(NO), are this specification's own statement; they replace
                         // R264 L53–L54's MOVED-against-HELD reading, whose matched arms R271 L16 removes. R264 L52–L55 is
                         // cited in this file for the THIS / NO form, the comparison and the not-observed case only.
                         // BECAUSE DG L20–L21, R271 L14, L16, L18.
  HOW(IF_THEN),          // IF SOME observed junction has SUBSTRATE(v) NOT_SAME RECORD(v) THEN the verdict is NO; otherwise IF
                         // SOME junction is not observed THEN MAYBE; otherwise IF_THEN. This specification applies the method's
                         // precedence (NO, then MAYBE, then IF_THEN) to the comparison's verdict, which is not the
                         // obligation's discharge. The verdict text carries the verdict word only; the run record names the
                         // junctions not observed. BECAUSE R264 L52–L55, W10D L35.
  FOR_WHAT(IF_THEN),     // The two columns are readings THIS / NO; the count behind RECORD takes "no weights, no costs".
                         // BECAUSE R264 L52–L54, DG L23–L24.

  WHAT(BECAUSE),         // "What it cannot absorb CANNOT stay" (FPP :138, as R264 L29 quotes it). The fold-effect commitment
                         // reads δ > 0 as what MOVED reports per junction and reads HELD as 0 (FE L126–L128, as R264 L23–L25
                         // quotes it). Composed by R264 (PROPOSE): what does not stay across the fold is the predecessor
                         // reading at each edit. BECAUSE R264 L35–L40, DG L15–L18.
  HOW(BECAUSE),          // The runtime overwrites nothing: it appends the successor's facts and retains the predecessor's.
                         // An edit is realized by a native ASSIGN field effect; the heat is what that discharge causes.
                         // The retained ASSIGN facts are the record of those events; the witness is their execution on the
                         // bound card, which no retained byte binds (this specification's reading of DSUB L12 for those
                         // facts). BECAUSE R270 L14, L16, DSUB L5, L12, SAY S12, R272 L10, L31.
  FOR_WHAT(BECAUSE),     // Reason this object exists: the shed is constitutive and is not written into records, so FPP's δ has
                         // no witness until a substrate observation is bound to the same tick and junctions and distinguishes
                         // the shed from discharge activity. BECAUSE DSUB L5, L12, R215 L15–L16, R264 L30–L31.

  WHAT(INSIDE_OUTSIDE),  // On link 2 → 3: the 468 retained readings (NO → NO) are INSIDE the successor field as they were; the
                         // 12 predecessor readings THIS at the edits are OUTSIDE it, kept only among the predecessor's facts.
                         // BECAUSE R264 L35–L41, R265 L13, R270 L16, R272 L16.
  HOW(INSIDE_OUTSIDE),   // Incidence := the flags whose site, edge or triad contains v. BECAUSE DG L21.

  WHAT(NEAR_FAR),        // Discharge activity at a location is every native discharge event there. The candidate shed is the
                         // ASSIGN class: twelve events on link 2 → 3 (Claude, PROPOSE, R270 L43–L45; the rules give the
                         // partition and do not force that identification).
                         // BECAUSE THERMAL_V014 as R264 L19–L21 quotes it, R264 L44–L47, R270 L43–L45, R271 L15.

  WHAT(CAN_CANNOT),      // The record CANNOT witness the shed; the substrate CAN. BECAUSE DSUB L12.
  HOW(CAN_CANNOT),       // An offline replay CAN qualify the capture against retained bytes and CANNOT bind an execution to
                         // the card; a re-execution whose record carries the binding CAN. BECAUSE R272 L27–L28, L31–L33, R271 L17.

  WHAT(MAYBE),           // A junction not observed is MAYBE, by name. This specification's rule: v is not observed IF the
                         // execution is not bound to the card (then EVERY junction); or IF the capture holds no ASSIGN effect
                         // naming v and does not hold the field effect of every flag incident to v (capture recorded
                         // incomplete); or IF the capture holds no ASSIGN effect naming v and holds a field effect naming v that
                         // is neither ASSIGN nor RETAIN_SITE; or IF no flag is incident to v. An envelope names exactly the
                         // junctions its flag is incident to (MUST, R_ENVELOPE).
                         // BECAUSE R264 L55, R270 L14, R271 L17, L18, R272 L31, L38.

  WHAT(MUST_LET),        // MUST: the expected RECORD bytes are fixed from the ledger before any execution. LET: measurements
                         // (cycle-counter samples) recorded beside the capture. BECAUSE R264 L78–L79, R265 L16, R272 L15, R271 L16.
  HOW(MUST_LET),         // MUST: ONE run record carries the same-run UUID / PCI / VBIOS / configuration binding of the card,
                         // ordinal / context, launch / resume identities, driver / runtime / boot context, allocation map,
                         // actual event-time capture / completion, the source / binary hashes, the input and returned
                         // states, the chain link, the event capture and the envelopes. LET: realization language.
                         // BECAUSE R271 L17, R272 L32–L33.
  FOR_WHAT(MUST_LET),    // MUST: the observer changes no native byte and nothing is subtracted from the capture. The first is
                         // shown so far on offline replay of the fact-commit routines only; both are to be witnessed on a
                         // card execution.
                         // BECAUSE R272 L24–L28, R271 L16.

  WHAT(TOGETHER_ALONE),  // The binding to the same tick and junctions and the distinction of shed from discharge activity hold
                         // TOGETHER on ONE fold, in ONE record; neither is the witness ALONE. BECAUSE R215 L15–L16, R264 L30–L31, L69–L70.

  WHAT(MORE_LESS),       // "The MANY's separation-content is MORE than the ONE's: δ > 0 (FPP Step 3)", done as "MOVED reports
                         // d_G(g₂, g₃) per junction … and which faces' ties break; HELD reports 0." BECAUSE FE L126–L128 as
                         // R264 L23–L25 quotes it.
  HOW(MORE_LESS),        // MORE by inclusion: the capture MUST hold every native event of the fold as executed, the ASSIGN
                         // effects among them (twelve on link 2 → 3), separately typed; no magnitude is read. Retained facts
                         // do not hold failed-match and interner attempts; an execution's capture MUST.
                         // BECAUSE R271 L16, R272 L16, L36–L37.

  WHAT(GOES_WITH),       // Each edit GOES_WITH every junction its flag is incident to; on link 2 → 3 the 12 distinct edits go
                         // with junction 17 (all twelve) and with junctions 15, 16, 18, 25 (four each): 28 junction references.
                         // BECAUSE DG L20–L21, R265 L14–L15, R271 L18.
  HOW(GOES_WITH),        // The run record GOES_WITH the card identity and the chain link of the fold. BECAUSE R271 L17.

  WHAT(MANY_ONE),        // MANY edits, ONE fold; MANY junctions, ONE comparison, ONE verdict. BECAUSE R264 L52–L55.

  WHAT(EVERY_SOME),      // EVERY junction of the product (30) carries a RECORD reading; SOME read THIS (five on link 2 → 3).
                         // BECAUSE R265 L14–L16.
  HOW(EVERY_SOME),       // EVERY junction is observed or is named MAYBE; none is dropped. BECAUSE R264 L55.

  THIS, SAME_NOT_SAME, NO, IF_THEN, BECAUSE, INSIDE_OUTSIDE, NEAR_FAR, CAN_CANNOT, MAYBE, MUST_LET,
  TOGETHER_ALONE, MORE_LESS, GOES_WITH, MANY_ONE, EVERY_SOME
};

law R1_WHERE :=
  IF WHAT(o)
  THEN WHERE(o);

law R1_WHICH :=
  IF WHAT(o)
  THEN WHICH(o);

law R1_WHEN :=
  IF HOW(o)
  THEN WHEN(o);

law R2_WHENCE :=
  IF WHERE(o), WHICH(o), WHEN(o), FOR_WHAT(o), FOR_WHAT(BECAUSE)
  THEN WHENCE(o);

// OBLIGATION WITNESSES (readings of this one object, not additional laws).
// O_SUBSTRATE_WITNESS_OF_SHED: the shed of ONE fold read on its own substrate against the record's edit set, as ONE joint witness. Each restriction below is a restriction of that one witness on the SAME fold, not a stage: R_RECORD and R_ENVELOPE bind the observation to the same junctions; R_CUSTODY binds it to the same tick (the chain link) and to the card, in ONE record; R_EVENTS and R_SHED_CLASS distinguish the shed from discharge activity.
// R_RECORD: RECORD(v) for every junction of the product, from the edit ledger by flag identity.
// R_EVENTS: the capture of every native event of the fold as executed, each with its identity, ordered supports, actual commit / parallel-work ordering and buffer identities, separately typed, with nothing subtracted; the observer changes no native byte.
// R_ENVELOPE: every field effect names all its incident junctions and no other, with their exact rows of the junction binding and incidence role; SUBSTRATE(v) is read from the ASSIGN and RETAIN_SITE effects whose envelopes name v.
// R_CUSTODY: ONE run record binding the execution to the card (same-run UUID / PCI / VBIOS / configuration binding, ordinal / context, launch / resume identities, driver / runtime / boot context, allocation map, actual event-time capture / completion), with the source / binary hashes, the input and returned states, the chain link, the event capture and the envelopes.
// R_SHED_CLASS: the shed of the fold is its ASSIGN class of field effects.
// REQUIRED: One run record on the bound card carrying R_RECORD, R_EVENTS, R_ENVELOPE and R_CUSTODY on the SAME fold, with the comparison of HOW(IF_THEN) executed on its two columns and reading IF_THEN. R_SHED_CLASS is an identification and not a content of a run record: it stays MAYBE until a bound clause carries it, and this obligation stays PENDING with it.
// STATUS: PENDING
// SUBJECT: SHED_ON_SUBSTRATE
// LAW_CLAUSE: FPP#L138-L138; FPP#L131-L138

// RESTRICTION READINGS (findings within their witnessed scope, recorded 2026-11-13; not discharge; records cited below: R264, R265, R270, R271, R272; LEDGER is named)
// R_RECORD        MAYBE here: Codex reports it built for link 2 → 3 (480 flag identities persist; 12 readings THIS → NO, 468
//                 SAME; junction 17 twelve edits, junctions 15, 16, 18, 25 four each, the other 25 none: R265 L13–L16). Its
//                 offline capture reproduces the 12 / 468 split and the junction set 15, 16, 17, 18, 25 (R272 L16, L19);
//                 R272 does not report the per-junction counts. It is read in this file when the second vector is
//                 executed on LEDGER.
// R_EVENTS        MAYBE. Built and qualified offline: 480 field effects with ordered supports SAME; 821,959 native facts
//                 byte-SAME with the observer attached and absent (R272 L16–L17, L24–L26). "Full CUDA matching, scheduling
//                 and resource effects remain MAYBE, BECAUSE no device or world execution occurred" (R272 L27–L28).
// R_ENVELOPE      MAYBE. Built and SAME offline: 480 envelopes, 1,080 junction references, 28 on the twelve assignments,
//                 ASSIGN junctions 15, 16, 17, 18, 25 only (R272 L18–L19; R271 L18). Not yet on a card execution.
//                 Whether EVERY one of the 30 junctions is named by at least one envelope is to be read from the
//                 envelope rows, which are not held here.
// R_CUSTODY       MAYBE. The retained execution's log names an RTX 3070 and does not bind that invocation to the card
//                 (R271 L17); the offline run record carries every device field as NOT_BOUND_OFFLINE (R272 L31).
// R_SHED_CLASS    MAYBE. The rules force 12 ASSIGN and 468 RETAIN_SITE effects; they do not force the identification
//                 (R271 L15). That the shed is the ASSIGN class is Claude's candidate (PROPOSE; R270 L43–L45), which
//                 R271 L15 places under 264's reading. R264 L42–L43 name "the substrate activity that realizes the
//                 EDITs"; the sentence before it, on an "act of changing that reading", is NOT_SAME the runtime (R270
//                 L30–L32) and is not relied on. The comparison reads ASSIGN events per junction against the edit set
//                 whatever this restriction reads; whether those events are the shed is this restriction.

// EXPECTED TERMINAL
// seed cells 31; derived 46 (41 layer-1 + 5 WHENCE); total 77; 15 carrier identifiers.
// PENDING: FOR_WHAT(NO), WHENCE(NO), FOR_WHAT(INSIDE_OUTSIDE), WHENCE(INSIDE_OUTSIDE), HOW(NEAR_FAR), WHEN(NEAR_FAR),
//          FOR_WHAT(NEAR_FAR), WHENCE(NEAR_FAR), FOR_WHAT(CAN_CANNOT), WHENCE(CAN_CANNOT), HOW(MAYBE), WHEN(MAYBE),
//          FOR_WHAT(MAYBE), WHENCE(MAYBE), HOW(TOGETHER_ALONE), WHEN(TOGETHER_ALONE), FOR_WHAT(TOGETHER_ALONE),
//          WHENCE(TOGETHER_ALONE), FOR_WHAT(MORE_LESS), WHENCE(MORE_LESS), FOR_WHAT(GOES_WITH), WHENCE(GOES_WITH),
//          HOW(MANY_ONE), WHEN(MANY_ONE), FOR_WHAT(MANY_ONE), WHENCE(MANY_ONE), FOR_WHAT(EVERY_SOME), WHENCE(EVERY_SOME).
// O_exec = empty
// O_next = { O_SUBSTRATE_WITNESS_OF_SHED }
// This terminal closes normalization of the specification, not its obligation.

// ENCODING OF THE VECTORS' BYTES (explanation; not part of any declaration)
//   One byte per junction. Column order 0..29 is this specification's; R265 L14–L16 reports junctions by number, and the order is
//   to be confirmed against LEDGER when the second vector is executed. Byte 0x01 := THIS; byte 0x00 := NO; byte 0xFF := not
//   observed (SUBSTRATE column only). Encodings, not numbers.
//   The comparison is HOW(IF_THEN) alone, on exactly 60 bytes: a RECORD column (30 bytes, each 0x00 or 0x01) then a SUBSTRATE
//   column (30 bytes, each 0x00, 0x01 or 0xFF). Other byte strings are outside this specification.
//   The second vector fixes the RECORD column of link 2 → 3 from the ledger: THIS at junctions 15, 16, 17, 18, 25. How a
//   SUBSTRATE column is produced is governed by R_EVENTS, R_ENVELOPE and R_CUSTODY, not by the comparison. The four
//   comparison vectors observe no device; their SUBSTRATE columns are constructed: SAME the record; NO at junction 17 where the
//   record reads THIS; not observed at every junction; not observed at junction 0 only. They witness the rule and nothing about
//   a substrate.

